--recurse
# Integration tests each boot their own ephemeral dev server. Running four of
# them at once under -j4 contends for memory/CPU on small boxes and amplifies a
# shutdown-time teardown race (P10.0). Run integration files sequentially (one
# dev server at a time) while unit/replay tests keep running in parallel. First
# matching rule wins, so the seq rule must precede the catch-all par rule.
--rules=seq=t/integration/*.t
--rules=par=**
